# What never enters a build context.
#
# This is the repository root because the backend image's context has to be the
# root: pnpm needs the workspace manifest and the lockfile, and neither lives
# in apps/backend. So the Dockerfile is at apps/backend/Dockerfile and is built
# with `-f apps/backend/Dockerfile .`.
#
# Nothing in `pnpm verify` reads this file, or the Dockerfile beside it. That
# is the same gap CLAUDE.md records for apps/backend/scripts/dev.sh: Prettier
# has no parser for either (`--file-info` reports `"inferredParser": null`) and
# ESLint sees no matching configuration. Recorded rather than closed.

# Build output. Every stage of the image builds from source; a host-built dist/
# is macOS-produced and would be copied over the top of what the builder makes.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
storybook-static/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. `.env` is gitignored, which is not the same as being outside a build
# context — a build context is assembled from the working tree, not from git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not needed to build or run the server.
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.claude/
planning/
docs/
apps/frontend/
*.log
.DS_Store
